// same way -- the sign of a zero argument decides the half-plane
// (`atan2(+0, -1)` is `pi`, `atan2(-0, -1)` is `-pi`), an infinity argument
// gives one of the eight multiples of pi/4, and otherwise `atan(|y/x|)` is
